WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.068
-Welcome back.
I'm here with Rosario Dawson.

00:00:03.068 --> 00:00:05.371
And we're about to play a game
called "Know Your Better Half."

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.373
But to do that, we're going
to need your better half.

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:10.143
So please welcome former mayor
of Newark and current

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:13.513
senator from New Jersey,
Cory Booker!

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.181
-Hello. Hello.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:18.184
She is definitely the better
half in this relationship.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.418
-I know. Okay, good.

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:20.886
Alright,
here's how the game works.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:23.422
One of you will wear
noise-canceling headphones

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:25.425
while the other answers
a question about you.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.959
Then you will take off
the headphones,

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:28.761
and we'll see if your
answer matches.

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.563
Make sense?

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.732
-Makes sense.
-Here we go.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.300
Rosario, the first question
is about you,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.336
so please put on your headphones
and play some music really loud.

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:39.505
Give me a thumbs-up
when you're ready.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.241
[ Laughs ]

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:44.043
I feel like it's working.
Okay, here we go.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:47.446
Cory, here's the question.
You both follow a vegan diet.

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:51.150
If Rosario ever had
a cheat meal, what would it be?

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.519
-I think that the one food
that she goes crazy over --

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.355
And we have a big fight
over this,

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.923
because she's from New York,
I'm from New Jersey.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.958
Jersey obviously has
the best pizza,

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.160
New York, the second-best
pizza in America.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.630
So I'm going to, unfortunately,

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.800
have to enter into
this debate publicly with her.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.067
But I'm going to say pizza.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.235
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.437
Okay, this is unbelievable.
Alright, alright.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:12.438
-Oh.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:14.640
♪ I just can't be polite ♪

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.009
♪ Don't worry about me ♪

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:19.512
-The question was,
"You both follow a vegan diet.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.881
If Rosario ever had
a cheat meal,

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.683
what would it be?"

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.652
-I mean, I'm a New Yorker,
so I'm always going to have,

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:31.657
like, pizza, bagel and lox,
you know --

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:34.093
-The best pizza in the world,
New York pizza.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.094
-Yeah. You got to be able
to get a slice.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.562
-Honey, honey...

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:39.032
-You know, it's great to have a
normal, regular vegan pizza,

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.099
but, like --

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:41.467
-Honey,
you know the best pizza --

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:42.568
Now that you live in New Jersey,

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:45.037
the best pizza in America
is Jersey pizza.

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:47.306
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.842
Just don't do anything.
Just bite your tongue.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:52.579
Just bite your tongue.
-What? I'm sorry. What?

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:55.548
-You cut out.
The Zoom cut out. Very good.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.850
Cory, it's your turn
to put on the headphones.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.719
-I'm going with
"Seasons of Love" right here.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:03.122
-Oh. Okay, here we go.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.424
Here is the question.

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.326
You two recently
moved in together.

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:10.163
What's Cory's
weirdest habit at home?

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:13.932
-He would probably say,
because he just started doing,

00:02:13.932 --> 00:02:17.136
you know, like, Wim Hof Method,
like, cold stuff,

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.472
so he's been doing
these cold showers.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.841
-Okay, here we go.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.976
-Am I good to come back?
-Yeah, you're good. Yeah.

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.979
Okay, the question was, "You two
recently moved in together.

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:29.849
What's Cory's weirdest
habit at home?"

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:33.686
-So, a big issue has come up
recently in the relationship

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:38.591
because I now, most mornings,
will take contrast showers,

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:41.127
where you stand
under ice-cold water,

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.662
but it has
a lot of health benefits.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:45.097
-That is a match.
That is exactly what she said.

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:48.500
She said the cold showers.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:51.104
Dude, you guys are crushing it.
Alright, you're 2 for 2 here.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.205
Cory, please put
the headphones on again.

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:55.174
Alright, Rosario,
this is the last question.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:58.911
What was Cory's smoothest move
when you were first dating?

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:05.618
-I don't know that I
would call Cory smooth per se.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.754
That's not why we're together.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:14.060
I find him very punny and clever
and passionate and wonderful.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.829
He, all for an entire year --

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.163
Especially
when he was campaigning

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:21.267
and I was taking care of my dad
and we were apart a lot,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:24.437
he would wake me up every day
with a song.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.604
So he would send me a song.

00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:27.073
So we have this playlist,

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:29.275
and, you know,
there's almost 200 songs.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.011
But it just would initiate
a conversation every morning,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.746
and then we would talk about
the song and what it meant

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.715
to either of us,
or if it was a new song --

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:36.916
It was just -- It was wonderful.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.818
Now we have a love playlist,
which is great.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.052
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:41.921
Everyone is freaking out
right now, going,

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.357
"Honey, why don't we have
a love playlist?"

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.759
Oh, my God. That is amazing.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.161
Alright, I can't wait to --

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.928
I want to see
his reaction to this.

00:03:49.928 --> 00:03:53.466
The question was,
"What was Cory's smoothest move

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:54.634
when you guys were dating?",

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.735
when you were first dating.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:04:00.406
-[ Laughs ]
That is an awful question.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:05.544
I'm sorry, because I'm not
the smoothest.

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:08.014
I'm not the smoothest.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.583
So, I don't know if
she would --

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.184
She probably just said
I'm not smooth,

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:14.420
but I will tell you,

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.589
I think I do things
that are sweet at least.

00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:19.559
-Alright, not only are you
in such big trouble

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:22.895
because, dude, she actually
said, "He's not smooth,"

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.296
which is what you said,

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:27.833
so you get points for that,
which is unbelievable.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.269
You guys are, like,
perfect together. But --

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.836
-But hold on.
What did she say, though?

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:33.072
She had to have said something.
I'm curious.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.908
-How about the love playlist?

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.878
-Oh, okay, yeah.
So, when we first --

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.713
-Now you know about it.
-He's good.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.481
-Now it's your favorite thing.
-I find that clever.

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:43.649
-Yeah, of course.

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:44.783
Thank you so much
for playing this.

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.518
That is
"Know Your Better Half."

00:04:46.518 --> 00:04:48.021
You guys crushed it.

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:51.257
My thanks again to Senator
Cory Booker and Rosario Dawson.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:54.427
"Go-Big Show" is on Thursdays
at 9:00 p.m. on TBS.

